-- title:
--   Commute GHalf Sandwich Split Succ Lift
-- statement:
--   **The split-successor lift preserves the operator relation.**
--
--   Let $(m,q,d)$ have a field model, let $\psi_{AB}$ be a bipartite quantum state, and let $r\in\mathbb N$. Let $A$ and $B$ be operator families on the move-chain question space $\mathsf{MoveQ}_r$ with move-chain outcome space $\mathsf{MoveO}_r$. Assume
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}_{\psi_{AB},\,\operatorname{Unif}(\mathsf{MoveQ}_r)}(A,B;\delta).
--   $$
--
--   Let $\mathsf S_r(A)$ and $\mathsf S_r(B)$ be obtained by reindexing these families through the split-successor bijections. Their questions are a slice question together with an $(r+1)$-tuple of points, and their outcomes are one completed slice outcome together with an $(r+1)$-tuple of completed outcomes. Then
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}_{\psi_{AB},\,\operatorname{Unif}(\mathcal Q\times\mathbb{F}_q^{r+1})}
--   \left(\mathsf S_r(A),\mathsf S_r(B);\delta\right).
--   $$
--
--   This is the uniform reindexing step used by the post-move flat-step construction.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.commuteGHalfSandwich_splitSuccLift`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Pasting/ComparisonLemmas/CommuteGHalfSandwich/MoveChain/Lifting.lean#L239-L303

